  "schemaVersion": "2.3.0",
  "name": "03 · Procurement workspace",
  "owner": "Fictional example product owner",
  "audience": "Product owners and delivery teams reviewing a fictional prototype",
  "goal": "Review a complete procurement workspace with independent request and supplier forms and seven purpose-specific lists.",
  "scope": "Two forms, seven list views, request line-item table and optional contact cards. Session-only CRUD, filtering, presets and validation. No automatic relationship between requests and suppliers, approval workflow or real identity.",
  "theme": "fluent",
  "languages": ["de", "en"],
  "decisions": "Stable form/list IDs separate requests from supplier master data. Planned roles: requester creates and maintains own drafts; purchasing processes requests and maintains suppliers; observer reads overview/directory. Current action switches are per-view capabilities for everybody, not role permissions. Presets do not hide records securely. Contact responsibilities are business labels only.",
  "questions": "Confirm the future role matrix: field visibility/editability, own-record restrictions, status transitions, parent-inherited group rights, create/view/edit/delete per form and list, role assignment and server authorization. What identifies the current user? No rights or user identities are invented here.",
